 "review": {
  "management_type_reason": "MBG・品種: 必要なら花の直後に（8月半ばまでに）剪定。早春に地際近くまで切って若返らせてもよい。木本の花後剪定なので B（'Summer Wine' と同じ）。夏前・夏の傷みの記述はないので機械の C を B に変更",
  "management_type_quote": "Prune as needed immediately after bloom and no later than mid-August.",
  "management_type_by_matching": "C 夏前切戻型",
  "heat_west_only": "中",
  "muggy_west_only": null,
  "heat_muggy_west_evidence": "[おぎはら/品種] 耐暑性；強\n[MBG/品種] Best in full sun in the northern part of its growing range, but appreciates some afternoon shade in climates with hot, humid summers.\n[MBG/品種] Purple foliage tends to green up in hot summer climates as the summer progresses.\n[食い違い] 欧米の文献（品種の記述）は 中 相当。おぎはら植物園の値を採った\n[RHS/品種] Aspect: West-facing or East-facing or South-facing or North-facing",
  "spread_evidence": null,
  "mixing_evidence": null,
  "silhouette_evidence": "[MBG・品種] Noteworthy Characteristics Physocarpus opulifolius , commonly called ninebark, is an upright, spreading, somewhat coarse, deciduous, Missouri-native shrub which is closely related to the genus Spiraea",
